event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":88,"item_id":"rs_079a42b7f225d9c5016ac9670248f481969e0eba14131a5b6c","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Considering testing approach**\n\nI'm trying to figure out if I have enough time to test by writing to a new file. Should I reuse existing helpers or create a new test to avoid duplication? It feels cumbersome to append and edit at the same time, especially if it makes things unique. I’ve noted that bash doesn’t write well, so I think I might edit and replace to insert the new test instead of appending it to the end."}

